IMPORT `lpul-trust`

-- Legal Profession Uniform Law (WA), with the Legal Profession Uniform General Rules 2015, trust money -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_wa_legal-profession-uniform-law-wa_baseline.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

-- Life facts are from the workbench scenario au/wa/cradle-to-grave-daniel/facts.json: Daniel is a graduate (d030, 3 Feb 2020)
-- and then an employee solicitor at Swan & Partners, "a Perth law firm" (2020-02 to 2031-02); d031 (24 Aug 2020) "Admitted by
-- the Supreme Court; a practising certificate"; d038 (4 Mar 2029) acts for a client in an arbitration. d031 came before
-- 1 July 2022 and is "replayed under the Uniform Law", as in the Application Act baseline. Everything else -- the gap between
-- admission and certificate, the offences, the client's money, bills, dates and amounts -- is HYPOTHETICAL.

§ `fixtures`

`the client's $20,000 on account of costs` MEANS `The money` WITH
    `what it is` IS `money on account of legal costs in advance`
    `received in the ordinary course of legal practice at the client's direction` IS FALSE
    `invested in the ordinary course to maintain or enhance its value` IS FALSE
    `determined under s 152 not to be trust money` IS FALSE
    `declared by the Uniform Rules not to be trust money` IS FALSE
    `received in cash` IS FALSE
    `a written direction to deal with it otherwise` IS FALSE

