§ `ss 129, 134 -- d038: is the client's money trust money`

#ASSERT `Is this money trust money` `the client's $20,000 on account of costs`
#ASSERT NOT `Is this money trust money` `payment of Daniel's bill`

#ASSERT `Must my firm warn the client that this is not trust money` `money to invest outside the ordinary course of practice` FALSE

§ `ss 137-143 -- d038: where the money goes`

#ASSERT `Where must my firm put the client's money` `the client's $20,000 on account of costs` EQUALS `into the general trust account as soon as practicable, held only for the client and paid out only on the client's direction (ss 137, 138)`
#ASSERT `Where must my firm put the client's money` `cash on account of costs with a direction to pay counsel` EQUALS `into the general trust account as soon as practicable because it is cash, even if a written direction says otherwise; then as the direction says (s 143(1))`
#ASSERT `Where must my firm put the client's money` `an award paid in to be passed to the other side` EQUALS `paid or delivered as instructed, within the time set or as soon as practicable (s 140(1))`
#ASSERT `Where must my firm put the client's money` `payment of Daniel's bill` EQUALS `not trust money: the trust money provisions do not govern it`

#ASSERT `Is the trust money safe from my firm's creditors` FALSE

§ `s 144(2)(b), General Rules r 42 -- d038: paying the firm's bill from trust`

#ASSERT `May my firm take its costs from trust money` `a bill unanswered for 7 business days` (Date 12 4 2029) EQUALS `yes: 7 business days have passed since the bill without objection (General Rules r 42(3)(a))`
#ASSERT `May my firm take its costs from trust money` `a bill 5 business days old` (Date 10 4 2029) EQUALS `not yet`
-- 30 days from the itemised bill (20 Apr) run to 20 May: not on 20 May, yes on 21 May.
#ASSERT `May my firm take its costs from trust money` `a bill objected to, itemised bill received 20 Apr` (Date 20 5 2029) EQUALS `not yet`
#ASSERT `May my firm take its costs from trust money` `a bill objected to, itemised bill received 20 Apr` (Date 21 5 2029) EQUALS `yes: the client objected but has not referred it on, and 30 days have passed (r 42(3)(b))`
#ASSERT `May my firm take its costs from trust money` `written authority and a notice of withdrawal` (Date 3 4 2029) EQUALS `yes: the client's instructions authorise it and the client was told first (r 42(4))`

§ `General Rules r 52 -- statements`

#ASSERT `Must my firm give the client a trust account statement` `the matter is complete` `an active ledger`
#ASSERT NOT `Must my firm give the client a trust account statement` `30 June has passed` `a dormant ledger at nil`

